This is exactly the right stage to learn fine-tuning. You've already seen:

✅ Model can memorize
 ✅ Small datasets can overfit
 ✅ Pretrained knowledge can compete with new knowledge

Now let's understand types of fine-tuning and when to use them.

Big Picture

Suppose you have:

Pretrained Model
      ↓
Need to adapt it
      ↓
Choose Fine-tuning Method


There are 5 major types you'll hear about.

1. Full Fine-Tuning
What happens?

All model weights are updated.

Original Model
      ↓
Change every parameter
      ↓
New Model


For a 7B model:

7 billion parameters updated

Pros
Highest flexibility
Can significantly change behavior
Cons
Requires lots of GPU memory
Expensive
Can cause catastrophic forgetting
Use When
Building your own foundation model
Research work
Very large training datasets
Beginner?

❌ No

2. LoRA (Most Popular)

LoRA = Low Rank Adaptation

Instead of changing the whole model:

Base Model
+
Small Adapter


Only adapter weights are trained.

Base Model (Frozen)
+
Learnable LoRA Layers

Pros
Very low GPU usage
Fast training
Keeps original intelligence
Cons
Slightly less flexible than full tuning
Use When

✅ Chatbots
 ✅ Company knowledge assistant
 ✅ Domain adaptation
 ✅ Most real-world projects

Industry Reality

Today most Llama, Qwen, Mistral, Phi fine-tuning is done using LoRA.

3. QLoRA

QLoRA = Quantized LoRA

Model loaded in 4-bit.

Normal Model
↓
Quantized Model
↓
LoRA Training

Benefits

Even less memory.

Example:

Model	LoRA	QLoRA7B	~16GB	~8GB
Use When

✅ Consumer GPUs
 ✅ Kaggle GPU
 ✅ Colab GPU

Beginner?

✅ Yes

Actually this is probably what you'll eventually use.

4. Instruction Fine-Tuning

This is not a technical method.

It is a goal.

Example dataset:

User: What is AI?
Assistant: Artificial Intelligence


or

{
"instruction":"Translate English to French",
"output":"Bonjour"
}


Teaching the model:

Human asks question
↓
Model gives helpful answer

Use When
Building assistants
Chatbots
Question answering systems

Examples:

ChatGPT
Copilot
Gemini
Claude


All undergo instruction tuning.

5. Domain Fine-Tuning

Teaching specialized knowledge.

Example:

Medical
Patient reports diabetes...

Legal
Contract law...

Qualcomm
SNPE deployment
DLC conversion
DSP execution


Goal:

General Model
↓
Domain Expert Model

Use When

Company-specific applications.

Real-World Scenarios
Scenario A

You want:

A chatbot for your college website.


Use:

LoRA
+
Instruction Tuning

Scenario B

You want:

Teach Qualcomm SDK documentation


Use:

LoRA
+
Domain Fine-Tuning

Scenario C

You want:

Create Llama-4 from scratch


Use:

Full Fine-Tuning


Needs huge compute.

Scenario D

You have:

Colab GPU


Use:

QLoRA

Fine-Tuning vs RAG

New learners often confuse these.

Fine-Tuning

Changes model behavior.

Example:

Be polite.
Answer in JSON.
Act as network engineer.


Good for:

✅ Style
 ✅ Behavior
 ✅ Formatting

RAG

Model does not memorize.

Instead:

Question
↓
Search Documents
↓
Give Context
↓
Generate Answer


Good for:

✅ Company documents ✅ PDFs ✅ Frequently changing information

